  "why": "the travel time model design note, \"Variability\"/\"What the plan uses\": with no samples at all, a leg's allowing minutes are its typical figure plus `max(3, 0.15 x typical)`, rounded up, and it is the allowing figure leave-by and the live travel directive read, never the bare typical (which is carried alongside only for display). This fixture is new for the journey store rather than a re-baseline: it names the two figures directly (`typicalMinutes` 40 vs `minutes`/`recommendedMinutes` 46) so a future change to the padding formula, or a regression back to the bare typical, fails here first. Captured a minute after leave-by (07:15, leave-by is 07:14) rather than exactly on the boundary, the same margin `tracked-overtime-keeps-return-leg.json` keeps. Re-baselined for `ranking-consistency`'s maximum-session break: each `write` session now reaches its own maximum and owes a 15-minute rest before the day plan offers it again, so the four sessions that used to run back to back are now each followed by a `none`-reason gap, pushing the last one later and shrinking the final horizon gap to match; the leave-by/padding behaviour this fixture pins is unaffected.",
